A||||2||NEPTUNE||CRACKING TAILLIGHTS||||1||
Z||000000||NEPTUNE||12-10-2001||04:15 PM||||The sun has caused my taillights (87 SE) to begin to get that "rock candy" look, like the sail panels on a GT. Short of replacing them, is there a fix for this? Maybe painting the inside with clear? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cyberkhat||12-10-2001||09:41 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">got the same prob.Kind of like a de- lamination around the edge of the outside tailight lens.Mine is right down the center where the left and right lens meet.Somebody got a fix for this?||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-12-2001||12:12 PM||||Sorry guys, I can think of no way to repair this kind of damage.  One thing I did on my 87 SE was to remove the lamps, disassemble them, cut 3.25 round pieces of masking tape and place them on the inside of the clear lens directly over where the bulbs are in the housing, including the backup lamp.  Then i spray painted the inside with flat black paint.  When dry I removed the masking tape and reassemble the lenses.  Gives a very unique and I think attractive look to the lenses.  This is a possible solution.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
